{"name":"Red Gravel","hex":"#b8866e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"gravel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small fragments of rock, used for laying on the beds of roads and railways, and as ballast.","A type or grade of small rocks, differentiated by mineral type, size range, or other characteristics."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply a layer of gravel to the surface of a road, etc.","To puzzle or annoy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gravel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gravel","blocks":[{"text":"Gravel is a loose aggregation of rock fragments. Gravel occurs naturally on Earth as a result of sedimentary and erosive geological processes; it is also produced in large quantities commercially as crushed stone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Gravel_on_a_beach_in_Thirasia%2C_Santorini%2C_Greece.jpg/330px-Gravel_on_a_beach_in_Thirasia%2C_Santorini%2C_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravel","wikidata":"Q133833"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg/500px-Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg/1280px-Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg/500px-Kiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sand and gravel separator in a gravel pit in Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKiesgrube_Bernau_2012_-_panoramio_(7).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Haciendajokioinen2.JPG/500px-Haciendajokioinen2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Haciendajokioinen2.JPG/1280px-Haciendajokioinen2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Haciendajokioinen2.JPG/500px-Haciendajokioinen2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A gravel road in Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaciendajokioinen2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thu